# Shell scripts must have LF endings wherever they were edited.
#
# Not a style preference: a script with CRLF fails on Linux with
# "$'\r': command not found" on the shebang line, which says nothing about
# the real cause. The installer is edited on Windows often enough that this
# has already happened once.
*.sh text eol=lf
# PowerShell 5.1 reads a file without a byte-order mark as ANSI, which mangles
# every Cyrillic string in it and produces parse errors that point at the
# wrong line. The mark is content, so the file is left alone here.
*.ps1 -text
Makefile text eol=lf

# Go and web sources are normalised too, so a diff is about the change.
*.go text eol=lf
*.ts text eol=lf
*.tsx text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.sql text eol=lf

# Binary, never touched.
*.png binary
*.jar binary
*.webp binary
